#%PAM-1.0
# EXP1-style host sketch ONLY — not installed by the demo image and not applied
# to any live Lightsail / EXP1 host by this repository.
#
# Intent (fail-closed MFA with named break-glass):
#   - Interactive users: primary factor (pubkey or unix) AND pam_ezkey required.
#   - Named break-glass account skips pam_ezkey (console / emergency access).
#   - Never put pam_ezkey on a path that locks root console without a tested bypass.
#   - Do NOT enable Duo-style failmode=safe inside pam_ezkey.
#
# Contrast with the demo stack in ./sshd (Ezkey-only + pam_permit): that stack is
# valid only for the disposable Docker SSH VM.
#
# Example sketch (adapt user names, order, and account module to the host):
#
# auth       [success=1 default=ignore] pam_succeed_if.so user = breakglass quiet
# auth       required     pam_unix.so
# auth       required     pam_ezkey.so conf=/etc/security/pam_ezkey.conf
# auth       required     pam_permit.so
#
# Or with SSH publickey as the first factor (sshd_config AuthenticationMethods
# publickey,keyboard-interactive:pam) and pam_ezkey as the MFA line:
#
# auth       required     pam_ezkey.so conf=/etc/security/pam_ezkey.conf
# account    required     pam_unix.so
# session    required     pam_unix.so
#
# Rollback: restore /etc/pam.d/sshd from a copy taken the same day; sshd -t before
# restart. Confirm Lightsail serial/browser console the same day as any cutover.
